  "title": "# Model switches need Brett's approval (Urgent, Opus) Brett Nov 3 2026 (voice), angry: a headless b…",
  "asked": "# Model switches need Brett's approval (Urgent, Opus) Brett Nov 3 2026 (voice), angry: a headless build (agent-swarm-fable-rebuild, PR #247) approved its own Opus -> Fable phase switch in the orchestrator (`orchestrator.mjs act approve`) because its brief said \"do every step\". Brett: \"It cannot be switching the model without my approval. That's not even a veto. That's an approval.\" New project rule (add to _claude/rules/RULES.md and the decisions log, dated Nov 3 2026): a build's model never changes without Brett's explicit approval. Approving a model-switch phase is an APPROVAL (Brett must approve; confirm policy), never a veto countdown and never self-approved by a session, agent, headless build or the orchestrator itself. A session that reaches a model switch stops there and asks. Enforce it: 1. orchestrator `approve` action (orchestrator-core.mjs apply + CLI + console server): refuse when called from a headless build / agent / Claude session (detect via the same source signals used for 'who asked' on approvals: X-Axhub-Source, AXF headless env, agent env); only Brett's own signed-in console click, or an axHub approval he approves, can approve a model switch. Record who approved and when on the phase. 2. Build briefs (orchestrator `brief`, deploy/claude-headless.sh guidance, agent job router): say plainly that a model switch needs Brett's approval and the session must stop and ask; remove any wording that lets a session approve. 3. A way for a session to request it: an axHub approval (confirm policy, not veto) titled with the build, the phase and from -> to model; approving it records the approval in the orchestrator. 4. Audit: list every phase approved so far by a non-human source (the store's journal), report them in the PR; mark agent-swarm-fable-rebuild's s7 switch as self-approved (not Brett's). 5. Tests for the refusal and the approval path; THREADS row (profile urgent); PR (push banner merges it). Rules: one session, no sub-agents. Don't approve any phase yourself while doing this. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
